
# Node HTTP transport: wraps the built-in http module. `serve` creates a server whose request listener converts the
# node request into our `request`, runs the uniform router (`handle-request`), and writes the `response` back. Same
# router as every other backend; only the transport differs.

dock load
  load <node:http>, name http

load ../http
  find server
  find request
  find response
  find handle-request

task serve
  take server, like server
  take port, like u16

  save listener
    call http/create-server
      bind handle
        task on-request
          take incoming, like request
          like response
          send back
            call handle-request
              read server
              read incoming

  call listener/listen
    bind port, read port
